{"title":"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(planar_cutting,_similar_to_1,_not_using_ratios_however)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (planar cutting, similar to 1, not using ratios however)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Six points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eb06dce22486a98af7416c4bd3bdd842cdf7da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie in a straight line in that order. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a point not on the line and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea4a433ccc176a6f5ea3ece00398f54afea87f19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=26, BD=22, CE=31, DF=33, AF=73, CG=40,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"475\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7afa6d54a088a535870e6c4d9adfa85bc333a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG=30.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/3394e807ac30899b45011110f0a204d5279c57d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BGE.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba5a80ea1caae7fb0677811375ba2bbe0e7f2f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G; A=(0,0); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); B=(1.5,0); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, S); C=(2.9,0); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); D=(4.2,0); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, S); E=(5.3,0); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); F=(6.5,0); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S); G=(3.7,3); label(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, N);  draw(A--B--C--D--E--F); draw(C--G--D); draw(B--G--E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b41177ba04f38a6e1b3d6165019de3b779bf43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27b9d5d2762ae18f3084beda0d121a603b07bac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=b$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf556909dbdb4c1c517b7e55c6721c5fc883b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d21ac5cee89104c1e10d47a511b4e3c4365bfdd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06730ff27fdeb9b704a3356745b2374da23645d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />. Then we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44df1d327a67ae92a2a36add0ed0bb0472fed8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e=73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469a8e1d83a8bb4bf13ffc761a63f2b63683ae50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b220180a8a46aea12c6768e7304976b8c3cf85c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c40813abdda276a1cbcba94e828bce6327a4985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d=31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/71399ab34ac764d64c72ed58468cdbee8a9f5747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d+e=33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />. From this we can easily deduce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c736427d9ca95d60dd2eafdcee246674b9d1ff25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3baef2c5ca913b7425075cb61fdf34eae68fbf9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+e=34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8983e1fd2d7cd60867fa94e247e4f54b857ddc0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c+d=39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />. Using Heron's formula we can calculate the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb1c46a4bc0b3bd51b0195ca541ef9ab39f0131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CGD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a37349eaf0eb0335f874d93c5d2312bb89f7971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(42)(28)(12)(2)}=168$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"191\" height=\"35\" />, and since the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e5d9fea5588733250608eedcb93996963d81e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BGE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee66dbd1f66b5f63f3e6d83de1d53439c56cbe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{39}{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> of that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb1c46a4bc0b3bd51b0195ca541ef9ab39f0131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CGD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e5d9fea5588733250608eedcb93996963d81e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BGE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> shares an altitude with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb1c46a4bc0b3bd51b0195ca541ef9ab39f0131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CGD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, we conclude they are proportional and we can calculate the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e5d9fea5588733250608eedcb93996963d81e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BGE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f551c565bc558eacb6c399ae6570273778c03dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168\\times \\frac{39}{14}=\\boxed{468}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~ Quick Asymptote Fix by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Eevee9406\" title=\"User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>, edited by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Aoum\" title=\"User:Aoum\">aoum</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 2 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need to solve for the lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.  \nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80e67527934e0557de487e6fdc23ea439b269b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d5f81f182d0b2c07569dfc7ce37b85d901cabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c125ae5c4c453e15e1cca88cbcf5135549137f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = c$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96977602198ae053b0dcdced951cfcc9f8cff51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d6740d2df8c836c1c2ff13a3e7752a1efa43239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />.  \nWe are given the following system of equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe974f832ce78f8dfc38dd962cff1f9876d6c34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b = 26, \\quad b + c = 22, \\quad c + d = 31, \\quad d + e = 33, \\quad a + b + c + d + e = 73.\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12bc73e575c6d56a27591da64c6e0d460bb4ce94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb7fbe2dfba6d39530a5bf35eb2c2f2f8bfc5b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d + e = 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> into the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aec8a70667072d84a1b17668290c90b7e2bea9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c + d + e = 73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2326ba90a770988a3d5f9f7890bc3ea59fff01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c = 14.\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb7642eb0aee1a4bb3eb6ccaf884b003268efe5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 18, \\quad b = 8, \\quad c = 14, \\quad d = 17, \\quad e = 16.\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Next, consider triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8eaa1f00e5356878084a11f2aca23152e0e21a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e7601df9e0120fd73bbab765b877ee67c5b9a535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/497e1c6e6d4aeac170a215a5e4a05168aa49370f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CG = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e04c764bb1b910ecb646e56fc4112758f81966d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />.  \nBy the Law of Cosines, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0ddcf28542a17cf15f5af9090122dfea1fdbb3cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CD^2 = CG^2 + DG^2 - 2 \\times CG \\times DG \\times \\cos(\\angle CGD).\\]\" width=\"412\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Substituting the known values:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/affab2c92ca74e55493cfc3d9e368c25e9093586.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[14^2 = 40^2 + 30^2 - 2 \\times 40 \\times 30 \\times \\cos(\\angle CGD).\\]\" width=\"355\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f54f4524af8100dc91a2b5edc2e414ad2f5ed6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[196 = 1600 + 900 - 2400 \\cos(\\angle CGD).\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6b96e87a249bc9c12c7acbf0784917bb2a04b3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2400 \\cos(\\angle CGD) = 2500 - 196 = 2304.\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83f7f7fbb684971889608e88dee4c81aa33c4fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\angle CGD) = \\frac{24}{25}.\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e25dd610e73016f2e6c59ea7e65e821e54f037a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle CGD)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/a/10a5786b65663e55e2330a47ecf32b4d8666d9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"19\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/1600aa8c1db2001baf5eb49e6400fdac8cc9dfce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\angle CGD) = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{24}{25}\\right)^2} = \\frac{7}{25}.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Now, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8eaa1f00e5356878084a11f2aca23152e0e21a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab0aa2643ee9ce5541f0fd9c2737c2283b92a02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\times 40 \\times 30 \\times \\frac{7}{25} = 168.\\]\" width=\"191\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Noting that the height of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8eaa1f00e5356878084a11f2aca23152e0e21a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as the height of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7d577fd284dbfa7307785794c013f8d87e7d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BGE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, the ratio of the areas of the two triangles will be the same as the ratio of their corresponding lengths. Therefore, the answer is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc8d7cb13b1f5a229feb40381689c7f1f9198769.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{168 \\times 39}{14} = \\boxed{468}.\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>(Feel free to add or correct any LaTeX and formatting)\n</p><p>~ Mitsuihisashi14, edited by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Aoum\" title=\"User:Aoum\">aoum</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28planar_cutting.2C_similar_to_1.2C_not_using_ratios_however.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(planar_cutting,_similar_to_1,_not_using_ratios_however)\">Solution 3 (planar cutting, similar to 1, not using ratios however)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (planar cutting, similar to 1, not using ratios however)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f47680738d71e4b2a108bd2e94cc778ffe31f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(12cm);  // Define plane vertices for a 3D perspective look pair P1 = (-10, -15); pair P2 = (85, -15); pair P3 = (95, 25); pair P4 = (0, 25);  // Draw the plane background fill(P1--P2--P3--P4--cycle, rgb(0.98, 0.98, 0.98)); draw(P1--P2--P3--P4--cycle, gray+0.5); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{P}$&quot;, P2, NW, rgb(0.4, 0.4, 0.4));  // Define coordinates based on the problem dimensions pair A = (0,0); pair B = (18,0); pair C = (26,0); pair D = (40,0); pair E = (57,0); pair F = (73,0); pair G = (58,24);  // Fill and draw the target triangle BGE fill(B--G--E--cycle, rgb(0.9,0.95,1)); draw(B--G--E--cycle, blue+linewidth(0.8));  // Draw the main line segment draw(A--F, black+linewidth(1));  // Draw given condition segments CG and DG as dashed lines draw(C--G, dashed+gray); draw(D--G, dashed+gray);  // Draw and label all points dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, S); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, S); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, S); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, N); [/asy]\" width=\"568\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>Consider the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that contains line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268cc1c279a785dfe605bfb8b514cbd85abebbc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 73$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. This problem is very lenient, as it directly gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, who sum to 57, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cbac1ca429d029729cd24a340cf0c137a002be3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> form a segment of length 55, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8cb515dc0f0737947c0a2773624daef6b33d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. It follows that then because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aad486159475661a998547fffde7c175737dbb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF = 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cbac1ca429d029729cd24a340cf0c137a002be3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e4f257f35673b9537155940e0fb906dfcba71ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee58baa715f461095a73b54bf32a3a0947dc419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e7601df9e0120fd73bbab765b877ee67c5b9a535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22bb2d247de3b247ba47de8d33a6a83990aefc92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7507d46afa6714fd34b8da071fcc4fd95f6066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4fe4e603244b20e756892b7f1e130113498912b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(14cm);  // Define plane vertices for a 3D perspective look pair P1 = (-15, -25); pair P2 = (90, -25); pair P3 = (95, 30); pair P4 = (-5, 30);  // Draw the plane background fill(P1--P2--P3--P4--cycle, rgb(0.98, 0.98, 0.98)); draw(P1--P2--P3--P4--cycle, gray+0.5); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{P}$&quot;, P2, NW, rgb(0.4, 0.4, 0.4));  // Define coordinates based on the problem dimensions pair A = (0,0); pair B = (18,0); pair C = (26,0); pair D = (40,0); pair E = (57,0); pair F = (73,0); pair G = (58,24);  // Fill and draw the target triangle BGE fill(B--G--E--cycle, rgb(0.9,0.95,1)); draw(B--G--E--cycle, blue+linewidth(0.8));  // Draw the main line segment draw(A--F, black+linewidth(1));  // Draw given condition segments CG and DG as dashed lines draw(C--G, dashed+gray); draw(D--G, dashed+gray);  // Draw and label all points dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, N); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, N); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, N); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, N); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, N);  // Function to draw clean dimension bars and labels below the line void drawLength(pair p1, pair p2, string txt, real h = -8) {     pair shift = (0, h);     draw((p1.x, h+1)--(p1.x, h-1), gray+0.5);     draw((p2.x, h+1)--(p2.x, h-1), gray+0.5);     draw((p1.x, h)--(p2.x, h), gray+0.5, Arrows(TeXHead));     label(txt, ((p1.x + p2.x)/2, h), S, fontsize(9pt)); }  // Add the individual segment lengths drawLength(A, B, &quot;18&quot;); drawLength(B, C, &quot;8&quot;); drawLength(C, D, &quot;14&quot;); drawLength(D, E, &quot;17&quot;); drawLength(E, F, &quot;16&quot;); [/asy]\" width=\"662\" height=\"332\" />\n</p><p>Triangle \\( \\triangle  GCD \\), has a height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that is shared by triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551b922a931c09d035800f66b06b3a9f1ddc5133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BGE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. The area of \\( \\triangle  GCD \\) through Heron's Formula is 168 square units. One can quickly find the height to be 24. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551b922a931c09d035800f66b06b3a9f1ddc5133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BGE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad4042666168a9a34affb64c63169f2f7105ff83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 39 \\cdot 24 = 39 \\cdot 12 = \\boxed{468}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"214\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathletes Corner\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cLIMq3LBQE0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cLIMq3LBQE0</a> \n</p><p>~GP102\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solutions 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98hzWL-cUvk&amp;t=6s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98hzWL-cUvk&amp;t=6s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II\" title=\"2025 AIME II\">2025 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-de